From cabf18d1c1a625af3a025c27c43cd46cd5112a1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 15:34:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland.drv: Use xdg_popup for transient popups

Owned popup windows should not be mapped as independent toplevels on
Wayland. Compositors can then stack them like normal application windows,
which leaves menu windows below desktop shell surfaces such as Plasma panels
and makes nested menu placement unreliable.

Map owner-relative popup windows to xdg_popup when the owner already has an
xdg surface. The popup positioner is rebuilt from the Wine window geometry,
uses compositor constraint adjustment for edge flipping/sliding, and
inherits the parent's scale state.

Also request activation of the owner toplevel before dispatching
StatusNotifierItem context menu callbacks and keep SNI-provided menu
coordinates away from screen edges. This gives applications a valid
foreground parent before they create their menu and avoids anchoring tray
menus inside panel edge affordances.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
